   "dry_run": "pump commanded on, flow sensor reads ~0 -> stop pump, raise fault",
   "sensor_failure": "missing reading for a required field -> fall back to bypass (safe default), raise fault",
   "rationale": "Hard requirement carried from the earlier contract. In the current model the shield acts on the TOP water node (start of sub-step) and on the PCM; plain-tank peaks reached 73.3 C in the multi-node model, below the 75 C limit (docs/PROGRESS.md section 6).",
   "note_v2": "Finding: the existing PCM-side shield only blocks CHARGING at 62 C and is not enough for PCMs already above their melt band; some designs exceed 65 C. A design is infeasible if its PCM peak exceeds 65 C in any simulated year."
  }
